      "text": "To solve the expression \\(19^2 - 17^2 + 15^2 - 13^2 + 11^2 - 9^2 + 7^2 - 5^2 + 3^2 - 1^2\\), we can use the difference of squares formula, which states that \\(a^2 - b^2 = (a - b)(a + b)\\).\n\nFirst, let's pair up the terms to use the difference of squares formula:\n\n\\[\n(19^2 - 17^2) + (15^2 - 13^2) + (11^2 - 9^2) + (7^2 - 5^2) + (3^2 - 1^2)\n\\]\n\nNow, we apply the difference of squares formula to each pair:\n\n1. \\(19^2 - 17^2 = (19 - 17)(19 + 17) = 2 \\cdot 36 = 72\\)\n2. \\(15^2 - 13^2 = (15 - 13)(15 + 13) = 2 \\cdot 28 = 56\\)\n3. \\(11^2 - 9^2 = (11 - 9)(11 + 9) = 2 \\cdot 20 = 40\\)\n4. \\(7^2 - 5^2 = (7 - 5)(7 + 5) = 2 \\cdot 12 = 24\\)\n5. \\(3^2 - 1^2 = (3 - 1)(3 + 1) = 2 \\cdot 4 = 8\\)\n\nNow, we sum these results:\n\n\\[\n72 + 56 + 40 + 24 + 8\n\\]\n\nWe can add these step by step:\n\n\\[\n72 + 56 = 128\n\\]\n\\[\n128 + 40 = 168\n\\]\n\\[\n168 + 24 = 192\n\\]\n\\[\n192 + 8 = 200\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of the given expression is \\(\\boxed{200}\\).",
