      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the value of the expression \\(19^2 - 17^2 + 15^2 - 13^2 + 11^2 - 9^2 + 7^2 - 5^2 + 3^2 - 1^2\\), we can use the difference of squares formula, which states that \\(a^2 - b^2 = (a - b)(a + b)\\).\n\nLet's break it down step by step:\n\n1. For \\(19^2 - 17^2\\), we have:\n   \\[\n   19^2 - 17^2 = (19 - 17)(19 + 17) = 2 \\cdot 36 = 72\n   \\]\n\n2. For \\(15^2 - 13^2\\), we have:\n   \\[\n   15^2 - 13^2 = (15 - 13)(15 + 13) = 2 \\cdot 28 = 56\n   \\]\n\n3. For \\(11^2 - 9^2\\), we have:\n   \\[\n   11^2 - 9^2 = (11 - 9)(11 + 9) = 2 \\cdot 20 = 40\n   \\]\n\n4. For \\(7^2 - 5^2\\), we have:\n   \\[\n   7^2 - 5^2 = (7 - 5)(7 + 5) = 2 \\cdot 12 = 24\n   \\]\n\n5. For \\(3^2 - 1^2\\), we have:\n   \\[\n   3^2 - 1^2 = (3 - 1)(3 + 1) = 2 \\cdot 4 = 8\n   \\]\n\nNow, we sum all these results together:\n\\[\n72 + 56 + 40 + 24 + 8 = 200\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of the expression is \\(\\boxed{200}\\).",
